Mia Wang: Quick QA: compact left nav + deep links  should we keep a tiny breadcrumb or rely on the header? short links sometimes drop workspace filters :thinking_face;
Jamie Lee: Tiny breadcrumb wins for landing context. If hidden, header must always surface workspace and be keyboard-focusable.;
Omar Khan: Agree. Routing contract: canonical path `/w/:ws/...`. On boot rewrite `/models/:id?ws=` -> `/w/:ws/models/:id` via history.replaceState so hydration + analytics align.;
Nora Patel: Accessibility: breadcrumb lives in a `nav` landmark, active crumb uses `aria-current="page"`, truncated crumbs include `aria-label` with full name. Mobile long-press should open an accessible sheet (role=dialog) with actions (copy link / open parent).;
Mia Wang: UX: condensed crumb = single line, ellipsize workspace; on widths <320px hide workspace and use sheet. Tooltip only for desktop.;
ux-bot: Spec published: https://redwood.design/ux/compact-breadcrumbs  canary planned. A11y checklist added.;
Jamie Lee: Hydration pseudo:
```
// on init
const u = new URL(window.location.href);
if (u.searchParams.has('ws') && u.pathname.startsWith('/models/')) {
  const ws = u.searchParams.get('ws');
  const id = u.pathname.split('/').pop();
  history.replaceState({}, '', `/w/${ws}/models/${id}` + u.search);
  telemetry.track('rewrite_ws_query');
}
// migrate hash panel -> query param
if (window.location.hash.includes('panel=')) { /* migrate & track */ }
```
Omar Khan: Also add `?preserveNav=0|1` for embeds; default 1. Emit `legacy_url_mapped` on rewrites for monitoring.;
Nora Patel: Microcopy: use "Open parent workspace" in sheet. Add visible label "Show path" for screen readers on the breadcrumb toggle.;
Mia Wang: I'll update mocks and post frames tomorrow. :raised_hands:
